<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's TAP sees return to profit in 1997.</title>
<headline>Portugal's TAP sees return to profit in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese state airline TAP-Air Portugal said that it expected to return to profit in 1997 for the first time since 1974.</p>
<p>Company chairman Manuel Ferreira Lima told a news conference that TAP expected a profit of 1.3 billion escudos in 1997 and 1.6 billion in 1998 after a loss of 10.5 billion last year.  </p>
<p>The company gave the following forecasts:</p>
<p>	  (In billions of escudos, minus sign denotes a loss)</p>
<p>					   1996     1997    1998</p>
<p>    Net profit/loss		 -10.5	1.3    1.6</p>
<p>    Operating profit		  8.9	9.7   13.3</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3113126</p>
